1 NOTE Audrey grew up on a small farm outside Dill City in western Oklahoma, w
2 CONC here she worked hard collecting eggs, milking cows, picking cotton, and o
2 CONC ther farm chores.  After graduating from high school, she worked for a t
2 CONC ime as a nurse in nearby Elk City at Community Hospital.  It was then t
2 CONC hat she met Don Wilson and married him.  They moved around a lot in the e
2 CONC arly years of their marriage because of his job on an oil-exploration t
2 CONC eam. They had their two children during this time.  (An amazing coincid
2 CONC ence is that, when son Michael was born in Houston, TX, the supervising n
2 CONC urse in the pediatric ward was the woman who had been Audrey's supervis
2 CONC or at the hospital in Elk City, OK.)  In late 1958 they moved to Albuqu
2 CONC erque, NM, so that Don could work for his father in his electronics bus
2 CONC iness.  She lived in Albuquerque the rest of her life, until she died o
2 CONC f ovarian cancer in 1998.  She was 68 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her birth certificate says born in Dill City, but it also gives residen
2 CONC ce of parents as Dill City, which I'm pretty sure is not correct -- the
2 CONC y lived on their farm near Dill City.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on her death certificate is Audrey Faye Wilson.  Cause of deat
2 CONC h was ovarian carcinoma.  She died at St. Joseph Hospital - Downtown.
2 CONT Headstone of her grave says Audrey F. WILSON, 1930 - 1998.
