1 NOTE After Dorothy graduated from high school, she went to a nursing school i
2 CONC n Denver, CO, for a time but did not complete it.  Then, she worked on S
2 CONC andia Base in Albuquerque for a while, but developed problems and got a d
2 CONC isability retirement from the Civil Service.  Afterward, she did typist w
2 CONC ork part-time for Walker Radio Company for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was never married and had no children.  She lived with her parents h
2 CONC er whole life.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died following a series of strokes.  She had fairly severe health p
2 CONC roblems for a long time.  She suffered from paranoid schizophrenia, and h
2 CONC ad to take insulin for diabetes from her late 20s or early 30s.
2 CONT
2 CONT
