2 CONT From the Denver Post, 22 Jan 1973, p. 19 (obtained from the Colorado Ge
2 CONC nealogical Society):
2 CONT
2 CONT Leonie W. Rinker
2 CONT
2 CONT Services for Mrs. Leonie W. Rinker, 99, of 1137 Sherman St., were Frida
2 CONC y at Howard Mortuary, 1201 E. 17th Ave.  Entombment was at Fairmount Ma
2 CONC usoleum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Rinker died Wednesday at Presbyterian Medical Center after a short i
2 CONC llness.  She was born May 3, 1873, in Marshall, Mo.  She attended Denve
2 CONC r elementary schools and graduated from East High School.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 27, 1900, she was married to John E. Rinker in Denver.  He died i
2 CONC n 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before her marriage, Mrs. Rinker taught school in Altman and Cripple Cr
2 CONC eek, Colo.  She was a member of the Gold Nugget Chapter, Order of the E
2 CONC astern Star for more than 60 years, and a charter member of S.O.O.B.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by a son, Theodore W. Rinker, Englewood; a daughter, Mr
2 CONC s. Catherine R. McGrew, Denver; a grandson and three great-grandchildre
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
