1 NOTE In a letter from Catherine (Rinker) McGrew and Leonie (Wilson) Rinker t
2 CONC o Michael Wilson dated 16 Nov 1966, they wrote "William Adair & Mary El
2 CONC izabeth Wilson were the parents of nine children, seven of whom were Ca
2 CONC therine, Benjamin, Leonard, Annette, Adair, Byrd, Horace Everett."  Mar
2 CONC y L. was listed in the 1850 census (only 8 months old), but not listed i
2 CONC n the 1860 census, so presumably she died young.  In a letter from Mary E
2 CONC . (Reeves) Wilson to Jeanette (Reeves) Leonard dated 17 Mar 1848, she m
2 CONC entioned a child named William David; he might be another child who die
2 CONC d young, born between Leonard and Mary L.  This would make nine childre
2 CONC n.  However, In another letter from Mary Wilson to Jeanette Leonard, da
2 CONC ted 12 Feb 1856, she wrote "it has pleased our kind and heavenly Father t
2 CONC o take from me four dear little ones", so it sounds like Mary had at le
2 CONC ast 11 children, of whom 4 died young.  Perhaps two of them were stillb
2 CONC orn and not included in Leonie's count.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In information from Ridge Park Cemetery in Marshall, MO, her cause of d
2 CONC eath is listed as "flux - old age".
