1 _UID 275F8975BB779B4F9CD24813BA22131F7766
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 JUL 2018
1 NOTE The Hotchkiss manuscript says that Micajah joined an adventurer named W
2 CONC illiam Walker on an expedition to Central America.  Hotchkiss quotes Jo
2 CONC hn Wilson (Micajah's father) as writing "Micajah has become a wiser and I h
2 CONC ope, a better man, having gained amongst the Walkerites a great name.  H
2 CONC e went away a wild and rather thoughtless boy weighing 220 pounds.  He c
2 CONC ame back a sober, sedate and thinking man, weighing 160 pounds.  He giv
2 CONC es evidence of great maturity of manhood."  Unfortunately, Hotchkiss sa
2 CONC ys that he was killed somewhere in Honduras on Walker's second expediti
2 CONC on.  However, "Bear Flag Lieutenant: The Life Story of Henry L. Ford (1
2 CONC 822-1860), with Some Related and Contemporary Art of Alexander Edouart (
2 CONC Continued)" by Fred B. Rogers (California Historical Society Quarterly, V
2 CONC ol. 30, No. 1, pp. 49-66, March 1951), in end note 172, says that Micaj
2 CONC ah died at Ukiah, CA, on 29 Oct 1862.  He gives the Mendocino Herald (U
2 CONC kiah), 31 Oct 1862, as the source for that statement.  This death annou
2 CONC ncement was also in the Sacramento Daily Union on 10 Nov 1862 (p. 2), w
2 CONC hich is available from the California Digital Newspaper Collection, cdn
2 CONC c.ucr.edu/cdnc.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Medocino Herald, 31 Oct 1862 (obtained from Fred B. Rogers' notes in th
2 CONC e John Wilson Papers, BANC MSS C-B 420, The Bancroft Library, Universit
2 CONC y of California, Berkeley, CA):
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sudden Death" - M. D. Wilson, Esq., was taken ill with a cold Tuesday l
2 CONC ast.  On Wednesday he was found to be laboring under an inflammation of t
2 CONC he stomach and congestion of the lung; and on Wednesday night at 11 o'c
2 CONC lock, he expired.  Mr. Wilson was a member of the Bar, and a young man o
2 CONC f more than ordinary talent in his profession.  His loss is seriously f
2 CONC elt in the community.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT End note 172 of “Bear Flag Lieutenant: The Life Story of Henry L. Ford (
2 CONC 1822–1860), with Some Related and Contemporary Art of Alexander Edouart (
2 CONC Continued)” by Fred B. Rogers says that Micajah attended the University o
2 CONC f Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The John Wilson Papers (BANC MSS C-B 420, The Bancroft Library, Univers
2 CONC ity of California, Berkeley, CA) also include a couple of short letters f
2 CONC rom Micajah to his father.  Here is my transcription of one that is fai
2 CONC rly interesting:
2 CONT
2 CONT Trinidad [California] 26th June 1851
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear father
2 CONT
2 CONT I arrived here yesterday from above with the intention of going down bu
2 CONC t there being a few of our old Company here we have Concluded to raise a s
2 CONC mall party and retake the Gold Bluff.  We generally believe here that t
2 CONC he Pacific Mining Company have given up their Claim entirely and we int
2 CONC end to go in <u>on</u> <u>our</u> <u>own</u> <u>hook</u>.  All of us we
2 CONC re willing to do anything in our power to sustain the interests of the C
2 CONC ompany, but they have acted through-out the whole affair like a set of <
2 CONC u>Jackasses</u> and we did not determine to do this until our last hope w
2 CONC as gone that the Pacific Company would do anything.  Keep this to yours
2 CONC elf until you hear more
2 CONT
2 CONT Your Son
2 CONT M D Wilson
