2 CONT
2 CONT Sudden Death.--Mr. Samuel Grove of Cambridge, died very suddenly, last S
2 CONC unday. He was in usual health at dinner, ate hearty as usual, retired t
2 CONC o his room, and some hours afterwards he was found on the floor, dead. H
2 CONC is spectacles were on, and an open book laying on the floor, close to w
2 CONC here he was found. He was some sixty years old—an old and highly esteem
2 CONC ed citizen, and at the time of his death, was residing with his son, Jo
2 CONC hn H. Grove, Esq.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the Sunday before 29 Apr 1858 was 25 Apr 1858, in agreement w
2 CONC ith other sources.
