1 NOTE The John Wilson Papers (BANC MSS C-B 420, The Bancroft Library, Univers
2 CONC ity of California, Berkeley, CA) include a letter from W. Grove to John W
2 CONC ilson.  This is my transcription of it:
2 CONT
2 CONT Guymas June 23rd 1860
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr Uncle
2 CONT
2 CONT We arrived here on the tenth of this month.  and expect to leave on thi
2 CONC s afternoon.  we have been detained in changing to [sic] Flag of the Ve
2 CONC ssel.  also her name from "Pontiac" to that of "Alamos"  Guymas is a ve
2 CONC ry pleasant place.  the thermometer stands at about 90° .  the Country p
2 CONC resents a very barren appearance-- at least so far as I have seen.  alt
2 CONC ho I understand there is a large amount of fine Country interier [sic]-
2 CONC - they raise all kinds of tropical fruit in this state -- the mines are s
2 CONC aid to be Very Rich.  all they want is American protection and enterpri
2 CONC se to develop the Country.  the Mexicans and Yaqui Indians are fighting a
2 CONC ll the time within a few miles of this place  the Indians routing the M
2 CONC exicans all the time.  word come in town the morning that the Indians w
2 CONC ere coming in to take the City to day.  which causes some little excite
2 CONC ment among the Natives.  however [?] I have no fear as the Am. Sloop of W
2 CONC ar "<u>Lancaster</u>" is lying here and will afford Succor if necessary -
2 CONC - the Indians say they intend to take the City before the Americans get i
2 CONC t  I have no news to write  I am well  give my love to Aunt Ann- Mary E
2 CONC liza- and little "<u>Kate</u>"  also all the family - when you write to m
2 CONC e please direct to (<u>Cau</u> [?] of <u>Dr</u> <u>W</u>. <u>I</u>. <u>
2 CONC Hill</u> <u>Alamos</u> - <u>State</u> <u>of</u> <u>Sonora</u>)
2 CONT
2 CONT Your Nephew
2 CONT W. Grove
2 CONT
2 CONT P S I am well  I have gained fifteen pounds since I left home-- tell Ka
2 CONC j [? not sure what the word is, but maybe refers to Micajah?] I will wr
2 CONC ite to him from the mine
