1 NOTE She is listed as Martha Snoddy by James Hotchkiss, but the marriage rec
2 CONC ord from Howard Co. lists her as Margaret.  I have also found Margaret S
2 CONC noddy, married to Robert Wilson, listed in some Snoddy genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From a posting to the SNODDY-L mailing list by Joann Tortarolo dated 28 M
2 CONC ar 1999:
2 CONT
2 CONT I found in the book, Old Saint Jo: Gateway to the West 1799-1932, writt
2 CONC en in 1979 by Sheridin A. Logan the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Armstrong Beattie (mayor of St. Joseph, MO) married Eliza Snoddy 1841 (
2 CONC in Howard Co., MO), and they moved to Huntsville in Randolph Co., MO wh
2 CONC ere he was a merchant for 10 years..and then moved on to St. Jo.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sister of Mrs. Armstrong Beattie was Margaret Snoddy who married Ro
2 CONC bert Wilson (US Senator 1861-1873). [Note, RW was only a US Senator fro
2 CONC m 1862 - 1863.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Armstrong Beattie took their son, James M. Wilson into partnership in h
2 CONC is bank, and after the death of Mrs. Wilson, her daughter Mary Ann was t
2 CONC aken to live with the Armstrong Beatties at their home at Main and Augu
2 CONC ste Streets, now the Memorial Home. It was there that Mary Ann Wilson w
2 CONC as married to Rufus L. McDonald in May 1855.
