2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel Moruza Hotchkiss April 22, 1925 - May 22, 2010 Resident of Lafay
2 CONC ette Isabel Hotchkiss passed away peacefully on May 22 in the company o
2 CONC f her loving family. Isabel grew up in Susanville, California and often t
2 CONC old stories about the close-knit ethnic community in which she was rais
2 CONC ed. Her parents moved the family to Berkeley so that their three childr
2 CONC en could attend UC Berkeley. While at Cal, Isabel met a dashing young m
2 CONC an, James M. Hotchkiss, Jr., and the two married in 1949. The newlyweds s
2 CONC ettled in Oakland and later moved with their two sons, Joe and Ed, to L
2 CONC afayette. Isabel poured herself into caring for her husband, recently d
2 CONC eceased, and her two sons. The four enjoyed many family vacations at th
2 CONC e coast, including their annual pilgrimage to Coronado Beach. A skilled p
2 CONC ainter and photographer, Isabel was known for her artistic grace. She s
2 CONC urrounded herself with music, art and theater and shared her passion fo
2 CONC r the arts with her family and friends. Isabel is survived by her broth
2 CONC er, Tito Moruza, her two sons, Joseph and Ed, daughter-in-law Rose Hotc
2 CONC hkiss, granddaughters Sarah Hotchkiss, Beth Hotchkiss and Marion Merril
2 CONC l, and two great-grand-daughters, Cheyanne and Samantha. In lieu of flo
2 CONC wers, donations can be sent to the Nature Conservancy, Planned Parentho
2 CONC od or the Contra Costa Food Bank.
