1 NOTE Newspaper clipping (newspaper and date not identified, but another smal
2 CONC l clipping identifies the wedding date as 16 Feb 1890, which was, indee
2 CONC d, a Sunday) from Katherine Cooper's scrapbook in the John Wilson Paper
2 CONC s (BANC MSS C-B 420, The Bancroft Library, University of California, Be
2 CONC rkeley, CA):
2 CONT
2 CONT COOPER--DENNIS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two Santa Cruz Society People Married in Berkeley Sunday.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Sunday afternoon at 3 o'clock, Mrs. Katarine M. [sic] Dennis, daught
2 CONC er of Mrs. Mary E. Wakeman, of this city, was married at Peralta Park, N
2 CONC orth Berkeley, to Harry C. Cooper, third son of William F. Cooper, an o
2 CONC ld and highly-esteemed citizen of Santa Cruz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Dennis has resided for several years in Santa Cruz, and, during al
2 CONC l that time, her social and literary talent, her good taste and her act
2 CONC ivity and energy have been used in the furtherance of church work, of p
2 CONC ublic-spirited movements and also in the large social circle which she a
2 CONC dorns.  She has been an active member of Santa Cruz Parlor, N. D. G. W. [
2 CONC Native Daughters of the Golden West] from its inception, and has held t
2 CONC he office of District Deputy and other honorable positions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry C. Cooper is well known in Santa Cruz, having been born and broug
2 CONC ht up in this city.  He is a successful merchant, a young man of the hi
2 CONC ghest character whose integrity and uprightness have never yet been que
2 CONC stioned.  Although quiet and reserved in demeanor he is a social favori
2 CONC te, and there is a wide circle of friends and relatives to wish for Mr. a
2 CONC nd Mrs. Harry C. Cooper all the happiness which springs from a true uni
2 CONC on.  It is pleasant to know that they will live here and that, through t
2 CONC hem, one more Santa Cruz home will make a charming social center.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Santa Cruz Sentinel, 5 Feb 1943, p. 1 (obtained from Newspapers.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT H. C. Cooper Of Old S. C. Family Dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry C. Cooper, a native of Santa Cruz and a member of the William Coo
2 CONC per family, closely identified with the early history of the city, pass
2 CONC ed away in Oakland February fourth, at the age of 80 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry Cooper was elected recorder of Santa Cruz county in 1898 and held t
2 CONC hat office for 16 years.  He was chief deputy recorder of Alameda count
2 CONC y for many years, an office he held up to the time of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Santa Cruz lodge, F. & A. M. [Free and Accepted Maso
2 CONC ns], and served as the treasurer for a number of years.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, the late William Cooper, and family lived on Front street, w
2 CONC hich was then the main street of the town.  The property ran through to P
2 CONC acific avenue, where a large orchard was located.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Was First Mayor
2 CONT
2 CONT Old-timers remember the old Cooper store, which was candle-lighted at f
2 CONC irst, and then kerosene lamps were installed as a great modern improvem
2 CONC ent.  The father, William Cooper, was the first mayor of Santa Cruz.
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years, Harry Cooper and his brother, Frank, operated a book an
2 CONC d stationery store on Pacific avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given To City
2 CONT
2 CONT Part of the present site of the court house was given to the city by th
2 CONC e Cooper family, and Cooper street was named in their honor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Cooper visited Santa Cruz a few months ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his widow, Evva M. Cooper, and a daughter, Mrs. Helen D
2 CONC ingwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services, conducted by Santa Cruz lodge, F. & A. M., will be held in th
2 CONC e Wessendorf mortuary Monday, February 8, at 1:30 p. m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Private inurnment will follow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Harry was married to Evva Marguerite Love in 1934, according to the Bem
2 CONC is Mohr Murray family tree on Ancestry.com (https://www.ancestry.com/fa
2 CONC mily-tree/person/tree/25909694/person/13894041885/facts).  Also, middle n
2 CONC ame of Clay comes from there (most sources just have middle initial).  E
2 CONC vva had previously been married to Ernest Hudson Bemis and had four chi
2 CONC ldren with him.  Evva donated most of the John Wilson Papers to the Ban
2 CONC croft Library of the University of California at Berkeley.
