1 NAME David /Wilson/
2 GIVN David
2 SURN Wilson
1 SEX M
1 _UID 2EE786748E3B4845A9659D93D5940EB0CA83
1 CHAN
2 DATE 31 MAY 2018
1 NOTE Birth date is from James Hotchkiss.  I do not know where he got it.
2 CONT
2 CONT The big question about David Wilson is whether the David Wilson who was a s
2 CONC on of John Wilson (mentioned in his will) is the same as the David Wils
2 CONC on who was a son of Priscilla McCoun Wilson and grandson of John McCoun a
2 CONC nd the same as the David Wilson who married Sarah Clark Hill.  I do not h
2 CONC ave definitive proof that these are all the same person, but there is f
2 CONC airly good evidence.  The evidence that Priscilla McCoun was the first w
2 CONC ife of John Wilson (and therefore John's son David was also Priscilla's s
2 CONC on and John McCoun's grandson) is discussed in the notes for Priscilla M
2 CONC cCoun.  A few other items are discussed here.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Some circumstantial evidence is in the family names.  First of all, Dav
2 CONC id was likely named for his uncle, John Wilson's brother David.  The ol
2 CONC dest daughter of David and Sarah, Priscilla, could have been named for D
2 CONC avid's mother, Priscilla McCoun Wilson.  Priscilla was not all that com
2 CONC mon a name, so this might be meaningful.  Some sources give daughter Pr
2 CONC iscilla's middle name as Catherine, which could be for David's grandmot
2 CONC her, Catharine Yancey Wilson (however, the best information seems to be t
2 CONC hat her middle name was David).  Next, it is very suggestive that the n
2 CONC ext two daughters, Mary Eliza and Susan Ann, are the same as names of t
2 CONC wo of David's half-sisters (daughters of John Wilson and Ann R. Pulliam W
2 CONC ilson).  And finally, David's oldest son, John, could have been named f
2 CONC or David's father, John Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Another item is a Power of Attorney, which shows that David Wilson, gra
2 CONC ndson of John McCoun, was living in Howard Co., MO, in 1835.  Howard Co
2 CONC unty is also where John Wilson had moved in about 1820 and where David W
2 CONC ilson and Sarah (Hill) Shipp were married in 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT "James McCoun & Margaret Walker & Their Descendants" by Maurie McCoun K
2 CONC limcheck (self-published, 1993; selected pages copied from microfilm ob
2 CONC tained from FamilySearch.org), on p. 218 of Volume II, has the followin
2 CONC g transcription of the Power of Attorney:
2 CONT
2 CONT I, David Wilson of the County of Howard & State of Missouri for good ca
2 CONC uses to me moving do hereby constitute and appoint Samuel McCoun my unc
2 CONC le of the county of Mercer & State of Kentucky my true and lawful attor
2 CONC ney in fact for me and in my name to ask for demand sue for and receipt f
2 CONC or all monies or other effects that may be coming to me in any manner f
2 CONC rom the executor or administrator or the estate of Lanty Holman - now d
2 CONC eceased who was my Guardian in the sd County of Mercer.  also to demand r
2 CONC eceive and receipt for monies & other property coming to me from the es
2 CONC tate of my Grandfather John McCoun who lived and died in the sd County o
2 CONC f Mercer & I also authorize my said attorney in fact to bargain sell an
2 CONC d convey make all needful deeds bargains etc to all the true estate tha
2 CONC t fell to me from the estate of my said Grandfather and to receive all m
2 CONC oney & receipts for the same that may bring making however the said rea
2 CONC l estate no other deed to the purchaser than a special warrantee convey
2 CONC ing all my right and covenanting agt. myself and heirs and I further au
2 CONC thorize my said attorney in fact to do all needful acts to carry the ab
2 CONC ove powers into effect hereby ratifying and confirming all the sd acts o
2 CONC f my sd attorney in fact in persuance (sic) of this power the same as i
2 CONC f I were personally present & did the same myself.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given under my hand and seal this 17th day of July Eighteen hundred and t
2 CONC hirty five.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID WILSON  (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT For information about Lanty Holman as guardian of David Wilson, see the n
2 CONC otes for Priscilla McCoun.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps the most important evidence comes from a deed in Howard County D
2 CONC eed Book 21, pp. 190-92 (obtained from Shanna Tait and Harold Kerr).  T
2 CONC he deed concerns the sale in Feb 1879 of some land that had been acquir
2 CONC ed by Robert & John Wilson in 1824.  The sellers were four couples: Dav
2 CONC id and Sarah C. Wilson of Howard Co., MO; David W. and Rosa B. Wilson o
2 CONC f Randolph Co., MO; Edward T. and Elizabeth M. Wilson of Randolph Co., M
2 CONC O; and William N. and Mary G. Reed of Chicot Co., AR.  There is a notat
2 CONC ion that says "David W. Wilson, E. Wilson, & Mary G. Reed being childre
2 CONC n of John Wilson dec'd, who was a son of Gen'l John Wilson" (punctuatio
2 CONC n added).  I would say that, with this context, it is pretty certain th
2 CONC at David Wilson, husband of Sarah C., was also a son of General John Wi
2 CONC lson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A settlement document that I received with the guardian bonds for David a
2 CONC nd John T. Wilson (see notes for Priscilla McCoun) is interesting but h
2 CONC ard to decipher. The document is dated 5 Nov 1833, and has a list of in
2 CONC comes and expenses. I'm not clear on whether it pertains only to David o
2 CONC r to both boys, but several of the items listed as expenses were purcha
2 CONC sed for David on 20 Oct 1827, as I understand it, including a horse and s
2 CONC addle. One expense of $10.00 says "By Cash pd. Robt. Wilson to ---- Dav
2 CONC id's expences to Mo." (I'm not sure of that one word.) It sounds like D
2 CONC avid, at least, was in Mercer County in October 1827 and was outfitted f
2 CONC or a trip to Missouri.  Perhaps he had been living with relatives (or L
2 CONC anty Holman) in Mercer County and this was when he went west to join hi
2 CONC s father.  Or perhaps he was just visiting.  Robt. Wilson might be Davi
2 CONC d's uncle -- younger brother of John Wilson, David's father.
