1 NOTE His father’s will mentions a son named John (actually it mentions three c
2 CONC hildren of son John, and doesn’t name the children).  "James McCoun & M
2 CONC argaret Walker & Their Descendants" by Maurie McCoun Klimcheck (Vol. II
2 CONC , p. 218; self-published, 1993, copied from microfilm obtained from Fam
2 CONC ilySearch.org) lists John T. Wilson as son of John Wilson and Priscilla M
2 CONC cCoun.  A Mercer Co., KY, guardian bond dated 7 May 1827 lists him as J
2 CONC ohn Tilford Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT His children's names come from a deed in Howard County deed book 21, pp
2 CONC . 190-92 (obtained from Shanna Tait and Harold Kerr).  The deed concern
2 CONC s the sale in Feb 1879 of some land that had been acquired by Robert & J
2 CONC ohn Wilson in 1824.  The sellers were four couples: David and Sarah C. W
2 CONC ilson of Howard Co., MO; David W. and Rosa B. Wilson of Randolph Co., M
2 CONC O; Edward T. and Elizabeth M. Wilson of Randolph Co., MO; and William N
2 CONC . and Mary G. Reed of Chicot Co., AR.  There is a notation that says "D
2 CONC avid W. Wilson, E. Wilson, & Mary G. Reed being children of John Wilson d
2 CONC ec'd, who was a son of Gen'l John Wilson" (punctuation added).  I was a
2 CONC ble to find those three couples in the 1870 and 1880 censuses.  I have s
2 CONC o far only found Mary in the 1860 census (more distinctive because she w
2 CONC as already married by then).  In 1850, they probably should have still b
2 CONC een together as a family.  There is a listing that is thought to be the
2 CONC m living in Randolph County with H. B. Owen, who would have been their g
2 CONC randfather.  There is a record of a marriage between John Wilson and Ma
2 CONC ry Owen on 14 Jul 1834 in Howard Co., MO.  I'm not sure if it is right, b
2 CONC ut I am tentatively assuming that this is the right marriage/wife.  See a
2 CONC dditional notes under Mary S. Owen and Edmund/Edward T. Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Owen Wilson remarried on 12 Apr 1846, so presumably John died befo
2 CONC re that.  Edmund/Edward was born on 23 Jan 1842, so presumably John was s
2 CONC till alive nine months before that.
