1 NOTE Listed in the Hotchkiss manuscript as Priscilla David Wilson.  Listed i
2 CONC n the Allen Family Tree on trees.ancestry.com as Priscilla Catherine Wi
2 CONC lson, which makes more sense.  On the other hand, she is listed as Pric
2 CONC illa D. Ewers in the 1920 census.  The 1920 and 1930 censuses and the m
2 CONC arriage certificate for Carl F. Ewers and Lillie A. Raffety all spell h
2 CONC er first name as Pricilla, but her gravestone on Find A Grave (listing f
2 CONC or Priscilla Wilson Ewers) spells it Priscilla.  Carol Rawles, a descen
2 CONC dant, says her name was Priscilla David Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT It looks like she may have been married by 1876.  I think that she and E
2 CONC ugene are listed together in the 1876 Missouri state census, right belo
2 CONC w her family (which included David, Sarah C., Susan A., Jno. D., and Ja
2 CONC s. W. Wilson).  It's not very readable, but it looks like Edward E. and P
2 CONC . D. Eures (middle initial is uncertain for Priscilla; it doesn't look l
2 CONC ike the other D's on the page, but I don't know what other letter it wo
2 CONC uld be.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Oregonian, 9 Apr 1936, p. 14 (obtained from Find A Grave, listing f
2 CONC or Priscilla Wilson Ewers):
2 CONT
2 CONT EWERS – In this city, April 7, late of 1136 SW Jefferson, Priscilla Ewe
2 CONC rs, mother of Mrs. Pearl Ray, Mrs. Mida Matkin and Carl Ewers, sister o
2 CONC f Dr. James W. Wilson.  Funeral services will be held Thursday, April 9
2 CONC , at 1 P.M., from Holman & Lutz, S.W. 3d and Salmon.  Interment Rivervi
2 CONC ew cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Note that many places call this cemetery Riverview, but Find A Grave l
2 CONC ists it as River View.]
