1 NOTE Notes on Doctor James Wesley Wilson from Karen Levin:
2 CONT
2 CONT Family was noted for its doctors, lawyers, educators and statesmen.  Gr
2 CONC aduated from the College of Physicians & Surgeons in St. Louis, MO on  0
2 CONC 8 March 1889.
2 CONT
2 CONT Practiced medicine for two years while at college. He also taught schoo
2 CONC l for 4 yrs. in the Wilson School House where his father had taught bef
2 CONC ore him.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his graduation from college he practiced medicine in 3 states:  M
2 CONC issouri, Arkansas and Louisiana.  He practiced medicine for more than 6
2 CONC 2 years; almost 46 of these years were practiced in Louisiana.  He was a r
2 CONC eader and student until the day of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a licensed physician and he was certified by Law to practice Med
2 CONC icine and Surgery by the Louisiana State Board of Medical Examiners - f
2 CONC or year ending 31 December 1951 (the year of his death).
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of pneumonia at the Homer Memorial Hospital at Homer, LA at 7:2
2 CONC 2 a.m. friday, 2 February 1951/  He was formerly connected with the Bas
2 CONC trop, LA Optical Company and was also a former resident of both Bastrop a
2 CONC nd Epps, LA.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to Louisiana in 1905, and had been a resident of Athens, LA sin
2 CONC ce 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per my father (but sketchy) he was previously married, a widower, and h
2 CONC e brought with him a daughter.  His new wife, Lillian a widow, was supp
2 CONC osedly the same age as his daughter when they were married.  He and Lil
2 CONC lian had one child each from a previous marriage, two natural children a
2 CONC nd also adopted two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry family trees also list Fritz Capples as a child; he was adopte
2 CONC d by Dr. & Mrs. Wilson.
2 CONT Karen Levin lists Fritz Rubin and Harry J. Wilson as adopted children.
