1 _UID BD827B1A4BEF0446B0ADCA02BFB3EF0BEDE0
1 CHAN
2 DATE 16 OCT 2017
1 NOTE Yreka, CA, Siskiyou Daily News, 5 Oct 2000:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adair "Butch" Wilson, former Yreka Mayor and civic leader, passed away W
2 CONC ednesday, Oct. 4, 2000 at Beverly Manor Convalescent Hospital in Yreka. H
2 CONC e had been in failing health for several months.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch was born in Winthrop on Aug. 20, 1909. Winthrop (now under the wa
2 CONC ter of the Squaw Creek Arm of Shasta Lake) was the site of the Bully Hi
2 CONC ll copper mine and smelter (one of the largest in the world).
2 CONT
2 CONT After graduation from Shasta High School in Redding, Butch went to work f
2 CONC or the Pacific Telephone Co. as a laborer. He began working for the Uni
2 CONC on Oil Co. in Arbuckle in 1933.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch married Della Ruth Larens on Sept. 12, 1933. They often spoke of t
2 CONC he wonderful love and care extended to them by the Meyers' families whi
2 CONC le they lived in Arbuckle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In January of 1936, they moved to Yreka where Mr. Wilson took over the U
2 CONC nion Oil Distributorship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch was first elected to the Yreka City Council in 1944 and served un
2 CONC til 1956, the last six years as Yreka's mayor. He was re-elected to the c
2 CONC ouncil in 1974 and served until 1980.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch was a member of the Siskiyou County Planning Commission from 1948 t
2 CONC o 1961. He served as chairman for six years. He was a charter member of M
2 CONC t. Zion Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch was a past president of both the Yreka 20-30 Club and the Lions C
2 CONC lub. He was a member of the Yreka Volunteer Fire Department from 1937 t
2 CONC o 1957. He was a member of the Masonic Lodge and served as Master of th
2 CONC e Howard Lodge No. 37 in 1947.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch was a Past High Priest of the Cyrus Chapter, Past Commander of th
2 CONC e Mt. Shasta Commandry and Past President of the Siskiyou County Shrine C
2 CONC lub.
2 CONT
2 CONT For the last 14 years, he compiled the monthly financial records for th
2 CONC e senior center in Yreka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch retired from the Union Oil Co. in 1971. After retirement, he drov
2 CONC e the school bus for the Yreka Elementary School District. He was an av
2 CONC id hunter, enjoying the outdoors with his family and long time hunting p
2 CONC artners.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his wife, Ruth, in June 1987.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butch is survived by his sons, Norman of Fair Oaks and Bill of Grass Va
2 CONC lley; his daughter, Linda Ellison of Yreka; a brother, Bill Wilson and h
2 CONC is wife, Anna, Ruth's sister of Tucson, Ariz.; Ruth's brother, Martin L
2 CONC arens and his wife, Virginia of Gridley.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also survived by his grandchildren, Lesley Ghidossi of Folsom, No
2 CONC rman Wilson, Jr. of Fair Oaks, Todd Wilson of Sacramento, Shannon Wilso
2 CONC n of Folsom, Jennifer Ellison and Martin Ellison, both of Yreka; and a g
2 CONC reat granddaughter, Kate Wilson of Sacramento.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held 3 p.m., Oct. 9 at Girdner Funeral Chapel. B
2 CONC urial will follow in the Evergreen Cemetery next to Ruth.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family suggests donations in the name of Adair Wilson be made to th
2 CONC e Shriner's Hospital For Children, c/o Donations Dept., 2425 Stockton B
2 CONC lvd., Sacramento, CA. 95817.
