1 NOTE The Hotchkiss manuscript says he had one child, who predeceased him.  R
2 CONC obert was left part of his father's land in his will, but a deed of lan
2 CONC d from William and Catharine Wilson to William Thompson in 1817 (see no
2 CONC tes for brother William) says that Robert died without issue and Robert
2 CONC 's share of the land then went to his brother David.  By the 1782 tax b
2 CONC ook (Land Tax Records for Augusta County, microfilm Reel 21 from the Li
2 CONC brary of Virginia; note that 1782 is the first year available), David w
2 CONC as paying taxes on the entire 461 acres so Robert probably died before t
2 CONC hen.  (Thanks to Doug Jenkins for the tip about the tax records.)
