1 NOTE The Bushman information says he was unmarried.  David was left part of h
2 CONC is father's land in his will, and then when his brother Robert died he r
2 CONC eceived the rest of it.  When David died, he left the land to his broth
2 CONC er William.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Following is a transcription of David's will (Augusta County Will Book 1
2 CONC 2, pp. 116-117).  I have added some punctuation to improve readability.
2 CONT
2 CONT I David Wilson, of the county of Augusta & State of Virginia, being sic
2 CONC k in Body but in perfect mind & memory, do make & constitute this my La
2 CONC st will & Testament in manner following, Viz, after all my Just Debts & f
2 CONC uneral Expenses are paid I give & bequeathe unto my Brother William Wil
2 CONC son all my Estate that I possess, real and personal, or any that I have a
2 CONC ny legal or equitable claim to.  Secondly I order my Brother William to g
2 CONC ive unto my Sister Letty Wilson a sufficient maintainance as long as Sh
2 CONC e remains unmarried, & also to give her fifty pounds in cash or propert
2 CONC y which Ever may best suit the parties.  I do Lastly appoint my Brother W
2 CONC illiam Wilson my sole Executor of this my Last Will & Testament, hereby R
2 CONC evoking all other Wills or Testaments heretofore by me made & ratifying & c
2 CONC onfirming this to be my Last given under my hand this Twenty Fifth day o
2 CONC f Jany. Eighteen Hundred & four.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed & acknowledged before us
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm. Steele
2 CONT Sam Doak
2 CONT David Doak
2 CONT
2 CONT At a Court held for Augusta County, January the 22nd 1816, This Last Wi
2 CONC ll and Testament of David Wilson dec'd being presented in court was pro
2 CONC ved by the oaths of Samuel Doak and David Doak, two of the Witnesses th
2 CONC ereto, and ordered to be recorded.  And on the motion of William Willso
2 CONC n the Executor therein named, who made oath according to Law and togeth
2 CONC er with David Doak his Security entered into Bond and acknowledged thei
2 CONC r Bond in the penalty of Two thousand Dollars conditioned as the Law re
2 CONC quires and it is further ordered that the said Bond be recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teste
2 CONT
2 CONT Erasmus Stribling, CC
