2 CONC tevens County.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Riverside Press-Enterprise, 14 Oct 1998 (obtained from their a
2 CONC rchive web site):
2 CONT
2 CONT Homeland
2 CONT
2 CONT Leonie Trickey
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside services for Leonie Eileen Trickey, 82, will be at 12:30 p.m. F
2 CONC riday at Olivewood Cemetery in Riverside.  She died of heart and lung f
2 CONC ailure Friday at Antelope Valley Hospital in Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Trickey who was born in Shohuilla Wash., lived in Homeland 70 year
2 CONC s.  She was a homemaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include a daughter, Patricia Faia of Homeland; four sons, Llo
2 CONC yd of Antelope Valley, Nyman Wilson of Hemet and Harry and Clarence Wil
2 CONC son, both of Riverside; five grandchildren, two great-grandchildren and a g
2 CONC reat-great grandchild.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of that article is messed up.  Nyman, Harry, and Clarence were her b
2 CONC rothers, not her sons.  I have no idea if the numbers of grandchildren, e
2 CONC tc., are right.  Also, it says that she lived in Homeland for 70 years, w
2 CONC hich would be back to 1928, but I know from letters that she was not li
2 CONC ving in Homeland in 1937, 1940, and 1941.
2 CONT
