2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN W. WILSON, P. O., Gilliam.  Is a brother of Dr. Robert H. Wilson, a
2 CONC nd was born in Lynchburg, Virginia, June 17, 1825.  When quite a child h
2 CONC e came with his parents to Missouri, in the fall of 1830.  The entire f
2 CONC amily located in Saline county.  He was raised on a farm, and after gai
2 CONC ning his majority, and after his father's death, he took charge of the f
2 CONC arm and continued on it until a few years ago, when he commenced a gene
2 CONC ral mercantile business in the new town of Gilliam, where he may now be f
2 CONC ound by all his old friends and associates.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It doesn't look like John ever married (or if he did, it wasn't for ver
2 CONC y long).  He was living on the farm with his mother and other family me
2 CONC mbers in the 1850, 1860, and 1870 censuses.  In the 1880 census, he was l
2 CONC iving with his sister Juliette's family.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT However, there is an entry for J. W. Wilson in the Slater City Cemetery o
2 CONC n Find A Grave, which might be him.  The birth date is shown as 25 Jun 1
2 CONC 825, which is different from the above biography, but close.  The death d
2 CONC ate was shown as 26 Sep 1985, but has recently been changed to 26 Sep 1
2 CONC 885.  He is not listed in the biography of his brother Robert in "Portr
2 CONC ait and Biographical Record of Lafayette and Saline Counties, Missouri"
2 CONC , which probably means that he was already dead by the time that book w
2 CONC as published in 1893.
