2 CONT MRS. MIDA MATKIN
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mida Matkin, 81, of 4004 No. 34th St. died yesterday in a local ho
2 CONC spital.  She was born in Missouri and had lived here 10 years, coming f
2 CONC rom Portland.  She was a member of Royal Neighbors of America and the C
2 CONC hristian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She leaves a son, Eugene, of Tacoma; a sister, Mrs. Pearl Ray, of Portl
2 CONC and; and a brother, Carl Ewers, in California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be announced by Buckley-King Co.
