1 NOTE The Oregonian, 29 Apr 1949, p. 15 (obtained from Find A Grave, listing f
2 CONC or Charles Marcus Matkin):
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of Charles M. Matkin, 68, who died Wednesday at his home, 1
2 CONC 821 SE 35th avenue, will be at 11 a.m. Friday at Davy Sunnyside funeral h
2 CONC ome.  Burial will be in Riverview cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Makin, Mo., Mr. Matkin came to Portland in 1904 and went to w
2 CONC ork for Warren Construction company, later becoming the Northwest Const
2 CONC ruction company.  He worked with the same firm until his retirement in 1
2 CONC 944.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his widow, Mrs. Mida Matkin and a son, Eugene L. Matk
2 CONC in, Tacoma.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on his death certificate is Charles M. Matkin.  Cause of death w
2 CONC as coronary occlusion.  He died at home (1821 S.E. 35th Ave.).  His fat
2 CONC her is listed as LeRoy Matkin.  The certificate also said that he had l
2 CONC ived in Portland for 6 years (or maybe it means at that address for 6 y
2 CONC ears).
