2 CONT Tacoma News Tribune, 29 Sep 1960, p. B19 (obtained from the Tacoma Pier
2 CONC ce County Genealogical Society):
2 CONT
2 CONT EUGENE L. MATKIN
2 CONT
2 CONT Eugene L. Matkin, 57, of 2226 Tacoma Rd., Puyallup, died yesterday in a P
2 CONC uyallup hospital.  Mr. Matkin was a retired administrative assistant at t
2 CONC he Tacoma Naval Station and was a Navy veteran of World War I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Matkin was born in Missouri and came to the Puyallup-Tacoma area fr
2 CONC om California in 1937.  He is survived by his wife, Helen M.; an aunt, M
2 CONC rs. Pearl Ray of Portland, and an uncle, Carl Ewers of California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be announced by the Buckley-King Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems doubtful that he was a Navy veteran of World War I, since he w
2 CONC ould have been only about 15 years old at the end of WWI.
