2 CONT Newspaper clipping (newspaper and date not identified) from Katherine C
2 CONC ooper's scrapbook in the John Wilson Papers (BANC MSS C-B 420, The Banc
2 CONC roft Library, University of California, Berkeley, CA):
2 CONT
2 CONT DECEASED.--On last Saturday a telegram was received by Mrs. George R. D
2 CONC ennis that her eldest son, Mr. Wm. J. Dennis, had died suddenly in Rich
2 CONC mond, where he was in the employ of the Chesapeake and Ohio Railroad Co
2 CONC mpany.  His brother, Col. J. Upshur Dennis, of Baltimore went on to Ric
2 CONC hmond for his body and arrived here with it on yesterday morning's earl
2 CONC y train.  He was the eldest son of the present Mrs. and the late Ex U. S
2 CONC . Senator Geo. R. Dennis and only 26 years old.  Thus, at this very ear
2 CONC ly age, ends the life of a young man whose birth and position gave the g
2 CONC reatest promise.  He was married in San Francisco several years ago and h
2 CONC e leaves a young widow with two little children.  His funeral, which oc
2 CONC curred at 4 o'clock p. m. yesterday, was attended by a large concourse o
2 CONC f the friends that his genial disposition had strongly attached to him.  H
2 CONC e was buried in the P. E. Church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It looks like this article was probably from a Maryland newspaper.  Usi
