1 NAME Edmund\Edward T. /Wilson/
2 GIVN Edmund\Edward T.
2 SURN Wilson
1 SEX M
1 _UID D972FA3A8699428B8C7FD680CBA8ACC6B1CD
1 CHAN
2 DATE 5 JUL 2018
1 NOTE His age is given as 8 in the 1850 census, 27 in the 1870 census, 34 in t
2 CONC he 1880 census, 57 in the 1900 census, 67 in the 1910 census, and 76 in t
2 CONC he 1920 census.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name is given as Edmund in the 1850, 1910, and 1920 censuses and on h
2 CONC is death certificate.  He is listed as Edward in the 1870, 1880, and 19
2 CONC 00 censuses and in his two marriage records (and in the 1879 deed that g
2 CONC ave me his name in the first place).
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund/Edward is one of the keys to identification of Mary Owen as John T
2 CONC . Wilson's wife.  Edmund T. Wilson was listed living with H. B. Owen in t
2 CONC he 1850 census, and there is a death certificate for Edmund T. Wilson w
2 CONC ith parents listed as John Wilson and Mary Owen.  The obvious question i
2 CONC s, is this the right John Wilson?  Well, the 1879 deed lists him as Edw
2 CONC ard T. Wilson, with wife Elizabeth M., of Randolph Co., MO.  There are l
2 CONC istings of Edward and Lizzie Wilson in the 1870 census and Edward (?) T
2 CONC . and Elizabeth M. Wilson in the 1880 census, both in Randolph Co., MO, s
2 CONC o I'm pretty sure they are the right people.  In both of those censuses
2 CONC , Edward's occupation is given as railroad conductor.  Then, in the 190
2 CONC 0, 1910, and 1920 censuses, there are listings for Edward or Edmund T. W
2 CONC ilson with wife Bettie C. (in 1910, his name was listed as Edward, whic
2 CONC h was scratched out and changed to Edmund or Edmond) living in San Anto
2 CONC nio, TX.  It's not certain that this Edward/Edmund is the same as the p
2 CONC revious one, but what ties them together is that his occupation is agai
2 CONC n railroad conductor in 1900 and 1910 (no occupation in 1920, presumabl
2 CONC y retired).  I think this makes it likely to be the same person.  Anoth
2 CONC er confusing factor is that the wife had changed.  In 1870 and 1880, Li
2 CONC zzie/Elizabeth was born in New Jersey; in 1900, 1910, and 1920, Bettie w
2 CONC as born in Kentucky.  I was able to find a marriage record on Ancestry.
2 CONC com for Edward Wilson and Bennie Harrison on 15 Dec 1885 in Denton Co., T
2 CONC X; I'm assuming that's a mistranscription for Bettie.  A possible probl
2 CONC em is that the 1900 census says that they had been married 30 years and t
2 CONC he 1910 census says they had been married 45 years.  In all of those ce
2 CONC nsuses, by the way, he is never shown with children, so I think he must n
2 CONC ot have had any children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on his death certificate (obtained from the John Page, Orange C
2 CONC o., VA family tree on Ancestry.com) is Edmund T. Wilson.  Cause of deat
2 CONC h was myocarditis (?).  Place of death was 1015 Broadway, San Antonio, B
2 CONC exar Co., TX (home).  It says that he had been living in that city for 3
2 CONC 8 years, which would imply that he moved to San Antonio about 1890.
