1 _UID 5500927A9F874F11BEA6F60A3F1834A57B2F
1 CHAN
2 DATE 31 MAY 2018
1 NOTE There are several marriage records for John Wilson in Missouri during t
2 CONC he right time period.  Choice of Mary Owen for John's spouse is not cer
2 CONC tain, but seems right for two reasons.
2 CONT
2 CONT First, Mary and children are listed with her father (H. B. Owen) in the 1
2 CONC 850 census (she is listed as Mary Fray, having already remarried and pr
2 CONC obably having already lost her second husband since he is not listed wi
2 CONC th her).  The children's names and ages are a little off, but seem too c
2 CONC lose to be a coincidence:  David T. Wilson, age 16; Mary G. Wilson, age 1
2 CONC 2, and Edmund T. Wilson, age 8 -- plus an additional child, John H. Wil
2 CONC son, age 10.  David's middle initial is off, and age 12 is high for Mar
2 CONC y compared to other censuses, but errors like that occur in censuses al
2 CONC l the time.  John H. presumably died relatively young, but whether as a c
2 CONC hild or as an adult I don't know; I just know that only David, Mary, an
2 CONC d Edmund/Edward were still living at the time their grandfather, John W
2 CONC ilson, wrote his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second, and what clinched it for me, are records for Edmund/Edward T. W
2 CONC ilson over the years.  See the notes for him for details.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pittman/Hill/Lentz Family Tree on Ancestry.com has quite a bit of i
2 CONC nformation on Mary Owen, and shows three marriages for her:  to John Wi
2 CONC lson on 14 Jul 1834 in Howard Co., MO; to Thornton Fray on 12 Apr 1846 i
2 CONC n Randolph Co., MO; and to Robert Currin on 15 Nov 1850 in Randolph Co.
2 CONC , MO.  (Find A Grave, listing for Mary S. Owens Curran, shows the spell
2 CONC ing Curran on her gravestone.)
