1 NOTE Middle name is from his WWII draft registration card, from Ancestry.com
2 CONC .  Just had middle initial elsewhere.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Santa Cruz Sentinel, 29 Jan 1986, p. 21 (obtained from Newspapers.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT SUNDAY WAS a day of note for the Dingwall clan.  Most notable, it was t
2 CONC he 96th birthday of Travis Thomas Dingwall.  Second, the sixth generati
2 CONC on member of the family had her picture in the newspaper.  Margaux Dani
2 CONC elle Miller, who will be one year on Feb. 7, was in the Sentinel's Babi
2 CONC es of 1985 presentation.
2 CONT
2 CONT "We have a lot of five generation lines -- you see that a lot," comment
2 CONC s her great-grandmother, Evelyn Morelli.  "But <i>six</i> generations?  T
2 CONC hat's pretty unusual."
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaux is the daughter of Troy Miller, who is in construction, and Sue M
2 CONC iller.  Troy is the son of Patricia Morelli and C.T. Miller.  Patricia i
2 CONC s the daughter of Mac and Ev Morelli.  Mac was in logging for 40 years i
2 CONC n this county and San Mateo County.  His parents were Roy Morelli and V
2 CONC iolet Dingwall Morelli.  Roy worked at the Santa Cruz Southern Pacific E
2 CONC xpress building for 52 years.  Mac's cousin is DeEtta Dingwall Carlin o
2 CONC f Caledonia Street.  She and her husband were in the office equipment b
2 CONC usiness for many years.  DeEtta's uncle is Travis, who turned 96.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Tom Dingwall family came west via Panama, says Roy.  They walked ac
2 CONC ross the isthmus, with mules, instead of coming across the Great Plains
2 CONC , then boarded asailing [sic] vessel for San Francisco.  But, a strong w
2 CONC ind caught the ship and carried it clear to Hawaii.  So the travelers r
2 CONC eturned on the same ship, and finally landed in San Francisco in 1852.  T
2 CONC hen they came to Davenport Landing and established San Vicente cattle r
2 CONC anch.
2 CONT
2 CONT One other note about Travis:  His wife was Helen Cooper, whose grandfat
2 CONC her gave the city of Santa Cruz the property for a courthouse, today's C
2 CONC ooper House ...
