2 CONT
2 CONT Three Arizonans die in accidents
2 CONT
2 CONT Three more Arizonans have died in traffic accidents, the Department of P
2 CONC ublic Safety reported yesterday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tamsin Judith Tena of Globe died in a one-vehicle rollover on U.S. 60, 2
2 CONC 2 miles east of Globe Tuesday night, investigators said.  They said she w
2 CONC as in a car driven by Clint Sloan Jr., 46, of Globe, who was in critica
2 CONC l condition at Gila General Hospital in Glove [sic].
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Arizona Republic, 30 Sep 1971, p. 50 (obtained from Newspapers.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT Tamsin Tena
2 CONT
2 CONT GLOBE -- Rosary for Mrs. Tamsin Tena, 36, will be at 7 p.m. today at Wa
2 CONC lker's Globe Mortuary.  Mass will be at 10 a.m. tomorrow at Holy Angels C
2 CONC atholic Church.  Burial will be at Rest Haven Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Tena died Tuesday in a traffic accident on U.S. 60.  She had lived i
2 CONC n the Globe area since 1948, coming from Portland, Ore.  She was a wait
2 CONC ress at Larry's Cafe in Globe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include a daughter, Cynthia Tena of Globe; her mother, Mrs. E
2 CONC lizabeth Burch of Miami; her father, Emil Hellem of Portland; a sister, M
2 CONC rs. Delvan Hayward of Phoenix, and a grandmother, Mrs. Pearl Ray of Por
2 CONC tland.
